- Story & Context: The EP closes with the mythical post-mortem of Captain Kren, a retired 1950s radar pilot who vanished into the brine after attempting to steer a ghost vessel through the harbor channels guided solely by the rhythm of answering foghorns and the brittle ticking of his cabin harpsichord. Recorded inside an empty grain silo overlooking the channel, the track builds through twelve continuous minutes of droning psychedelic guitar fuzz and sub-audible house pulsations that replicate the spatial vertigo of zero visibility. Over the final decaying chord of the harpsichord dissolving into tape flutter, Kren's recovered voice log cracks through the hydrophone: "I gave the whistle two long blasts, but only the deep water answered."
